course: dictionary
lesson: 10848
title: Animals and their words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Scientists give animals names, and a name often tells us a lot. A vervet is a small monkey that lives in Africa. Read the clues in the words around it: «Vervet monkeys live in groups in the savannas and woodlands of eastern and southern Africa.» Savannas are wide, grassy lands, so that clue helps you picture where vervets live.
explain: Context helps you work out meaning too. «Vervet monkeys have different alarm calls for leopards, eagles and snakes» tells you the monkeys warn each other about danger. An alarm call is a warning sound. The words leopards, eagles and snakes are clues to what the monkeys are scared of.
explain: Look for the words that show what is different. «At the leopard call they run up trees, at the eagle call they dive into bushes, and at the snake call they stand and look at the ground.» Each danger gets a different reaction, so each call means something different.
fact: A vervet is a small African monkey.
fact: A vervet has a grey-green or silvery coat, a black face fringed with white fur, and a long tail.
fact: Vervets live in groups in the savannas and woodlands of eastern and southern Africa.
fact: Vervets have different alarm calls for leopards, eagles and snakes.
fact: «Savannas» means wide, grassy lands with few trees.
exercise: What kind of animal is a vervet? | A bird that flies over the savanna | A snake that lives in trees | *A small African monkey | A large grey elephant
exercise: «Vervet monkeys live in groups in the savannas and woodlands of eastern and southern Africa.» Find and copy one word that means wide, grassy lands. | *savannas | monkeys | groups | vervets
exercise: «Vervet monkeys have different alarm calls for leopards, eagles and snakes.» What is an alarm call? | *A warning sound that tells others about danger | A sound that means food is ready | A call to make a friend come and play | A song the monkeys sing at dinner
test: Where do vervets live? | On islands in the Pacific Ocean | *In groups in the savannas and woodlands of eastern and southern Africa | In the cold forests of northern Europe | Deep under the sea
test: «At the snake call they stand and look at the ground.» What do vervets do at the snake call? | Dive into bushes | Sing a happy song | *Stand and look at the ground | Run up trees
exam: Why do vervets have different alarm calls? | To show they are hungry | *Because each danger attacks in a different way, so each needs a different reaction | Because they cannot make any other sounds | To make the eagles come closer
